# Client-side routing fallback.
#
# React Router owns the URL after the first load, so a reload of /stats asks the
# static host for a file that does not exist. Serving index.html for anything
# unmatched lets the app resolve the route itself — and keeps shared links
# (spectator brackets, stats boards) working when opened cold.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the URL must stay as it was, or the router never sees it.
/*    /index.html   200
